# Changelog

All notable changes to **4Term** will be documented in this file.

## [1.0.0] - 2025-06-15

### Added
 - Initial release of **4Term**

## [1.1.0] - 2025-06-17

### Added
 - DTR and RTS control in the menu strip
 - Auto macro sending feature
 
### Changed
 - Main form layout and design
 - Serial options form 
 - Settings form
 - Macro set styling
 - XML file handling
 - Serial port handling
 - Settings handling

## [1.2.0] - 2025-06-24
 
### Changed
 - Removed unused code and redundant comments
 - Refactored functions for better readability and efficiency
 - Simplified assembly attribute accessors with helper methods
 - Improved naming conventions and consistent formatting
 - Updated comments for clarity and better documentation
 - Removed deprecated methods and fixed minor bugs

## [1.3.0] - 2025-07-02

### Added
 - AutoUpdater

## [1.3.1] - 2025-07-03

### Fixed
 - AutoUpdater reliability issues

## [1.3.2] - 2025-07-10

### Fixed
 - ComboBox in SerialOptionsForm

## [1.4.0] - 2025-07-17

### Added
 - Built-in update functionality integrated directly into the application for seamless update management
 - Support for external tools to enhance functionality and extend features

### Changed
 - Updated project to target .NET Framework 4.8.1
 - Updated .gitignore
 - Settings form
 - Main form layout and design
 - Settings handling
 
### Removed
 - AutoUpdater

## [1.5.0] - 2025-11-21

### Removed
 - Application update capability due to security concerns and to improve application safety
 - Unused functions in XML handling code
 - Unstable external tools feature

### Changed
 - Increased size of the Minus button
 - Increased size of the Plus button
 - Improved and reorganised the Settings form layout and code
 - COM port selection logic refactored to support dynamic updates without closing the dropdown
 - Macro navigation updated to support 256 commands across 2 pages instead of 512 commands across 4 pages
 
### Fixed
 - XML saving now uses <ItemX></ItemX> for empty elements to ensure proper structure
 - Main form no longer resizes after the Settings form is closed

## [1.5.6] - 2026-01-18

### Added
 - SwapButton now can be hidden.

### Changed
 - Returned old welcome message colors.
 - Removed a loop prevent delay.
 - Bolded program name and version in About Form.
 - Added experimental script loading.

## [2.0.0] - 2026-11-01

### Added
 - Macro buffer: edits the 16 macros of a page at once, shown over the output window (F9 or right-click a macro button), with Save, Revert, tags for changed lines, problems, scripts and risky commands, and a strip with the latest output.
 - Repeat interval per macro, set in the macro buffer; clicking the macro's button starts and stops the repeat. View > Stop Repeats (Ctrl+Shift+R).
 - Keyboard shortcuts for the macro buttons: Ctrl+1..8 and Ctrl+Shift+1..8.
 - Tooltips on the macro buttons with their commands; marks for repeating, script and risky macros.
 - Hex view with offsets and a text column (Ctrl+Shift+H).
 - Output log size limit (RichTextBox/MaxLogMB).
 - High-DPI awareness on Windows.
 - Timestamps at the start of output lines (View > Timestamps, Ctrl+Shift+T; off by default).
 - Logging the output to a file as it arrives (File > Log to File, Ctrl+L; File > Log File).
 - Find in the output (Edit > Find, Ctrl+F; F3 and Shift+F3).
 - Highlighting: up to 64 rules that color output lines containing a text, or only the text itself, edited over the output like the macro buffer (View > Highlights, F7).

### Changed
 - Risky commands (MacroBuffer/RiskyCommands) are never repeated.
 - Script delays must be 0 ms or more.
 - Code comments follow the GNU style; settings are kept in one table.

### Removed
 - M1 to M5 repeat menus and Advanced mode (replaced by per-macro repeats).
 - The old one-macro editor panel and the ExternalTools setting.

### Fixed
 - Many stability fixes in the serial port handling, settings and scripts.

